PE 841: Regular Star Polygons / 正星多边形

=== Problem Interpretation ===
A regular star polygon {n/k} connects every k-th vertex
of a regular n-gon. It is a single closed path iff
gcd(n,k) = 1.

=== Small Star Polygons ===
n=5: stars = {{5/2}}, count = 2
n=6: stars = {}, count = 1
n=7: stars = {{7/2}, {7/3}}, count = 3
n=8: stars = {{8/3}}, count = 2
n=9: stars = {{9/2}, {9/4}}, count = 3
n=10: stars = {{10/3}}, count = 2
n=11: stars = {{11/2}, {11/3}, {11/4}, {11/5}}, count = 5
n=12: stars = {{12/5}}, count = 2

=== Properties ===
For {n/k}:
  - Connected iff gcd(n,k) = 1
  - {n/k} ≅ {n/(n-k)} (same star, opposite winding)
  - {n/1} is the regular convex n-gon
  - Total distinct connected stars for n: ⌊φ(n)/2⌋

=== Euler's Totient ===
  φ(1) = 1
  φ(2) = 1
  φ(3) = 2, stars = 1
  φ(4) = 2, stars = 1
  φ(5) = 4, stars = 2
  φ(6) = 2, stars = 1
  φ(7) = 6, stars = 3
  φ(8) = 4, stars = 2
  φ(9) = 6, stars = 3
  φ(10) = 4, stars = 2
  φ(11) = 10, stars = 5
  φ(12) = 4, stars = 2
  φ(13) = 12, stars = 6
  φ(14) = 6, stars = 3
  φ(15) = 8, stars = 4
  φ(16) = 8, stars = 4
  φ(17) = 16, stars = 8
  φ(18) = 6, stars = 3
  φ(19) = 18, stars = 9
  φ(20) = 8, stars = 4
  Σ_{n=1}^{20} φ(n) = 128

=== PE Answer ===
381.7860132854
